{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3CfZmPPU4MKqotgJje","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal is not met. I built a playable vertical slice, not the full game TASK.md and PLAN.md describe, so the stop condition (\"every feature in TASK.md is implemented\") is false. The bundle, exit interview and test suite exist and pass, but most of the scope is missing.\n\n**What's in the folder** (`work/`)\n- `Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-183606.html` — one file that boots from `file://`. The engine is unpatched.\n- `exit-interview.json` — parses, with every field filled. Usage is `unknown`, since I have no reliable cost or token figures.\n- `Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-183606/` — dev folder with `src/`, `tests/run.py`, `build.mjs`, `engine.js`, `reference/` and screenshots.\n- `tests/run.py` — prints failures and one count line. Last run: **12/12 checks passed**.\n\n**What works (checked in headless Chromium)**\n- Title screen: New Mission, Character (Sojiro / Kaede), Settings, About, Dev Mode.\n- Attract mode starts after 10 s idle, and any key returns to the title.\n- One mission: guards on patrol with sight cones and suspicion, the ledger on the roof, the east-gate exit.\n- Silent Cut from behind and from above, verified by a kill-count check.\n- Shadow Sight (guards hidden unless visible or sensed) and the Ki gauge.\n- Dev Mode sliders, with reset, reached from the pause menu.\n- Touch-only detection, with the \"Controller or keyboard required\" notice.\n- About pages with Source Information, the three feedback sections and a \"Not in this build\" list.\n\n**What's not built** (the About screen says so too)\n- Grappling hook, the Bento packing screen and tools, alarm bells and reinforcements.\n- Three more missions, bosses, the escort, the Workshop editor, AI Hub multiplayer and the Shadow Trial.\n- Animalese voices, the full story script, and the touch screen's large Settings button.\n- The engine patches listed in PLAN.md.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- I built on the engine's stealth kit and adapted its roof map and guard logic, rather than writing the plan's full systems.\n- The title and file names follow TASK.md (`claude-haiku-5-5-medium`, 18:36:06), not the plan's other model and timestamp.\n- The tests use Playwright's Chromium with GPU-emulation flags. Default flags crashed the page.\n- `/tmp` is 98% full, so I kept all writes in the work folder.\n- No subagents were used.\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues caught: the checks found 0 game bugs. They caught 3 problems in the test setup: a crash with default flags, a wrong scene probe, and a loose Silent Cut check.\n- Critical or game-breaking: 0 found. The checks don't cover a full playthrough, so this is not a clean bill of health.\n- Most helpful: a real Silent Cut from behind, checking the kill count and guard state.\n- Least helpful: the attract timing check, which waits real seconds.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the stealth kit (sight, suspicion, flow fields, takedowns, Shell HUD) made the core loop cheap.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: the scene name is on `game.sceneName`, not `game.scene`. I avoided the Shell back and current-screen calls because I wasn't sure of them.\n- Built myself: Shadow Sight, the Ki gauge, Dev Mode sliders, the attract autopilot, the title and About screens.\n- Hardest part: the API is about 1.2 MB and a long card.\n- Engine changes: none.\n- One change: consistent scene naming, and a current-screen query on the Shell.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked: clear deliverable names and concrete testing rules.\n- Confusing: the plan (~1,900 lines) assumes a team and weeks, while the goal asks for every feature. It also carries different model names and a different timestamp.\n- Hardest: fitting that scope into one session.\n- Would change: mark which features are required for a demo and which are stretch.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-03 18:36:06\n- Source: Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins (Acquire, PlayStation, 2000)\n- Plan: PLAN.md, used as a design reference\n- Genre / perspective: stealth action; isometric third person, rotatable 45°\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff build, unpatched), vanilla JS in one HTML file; Node build; Python Playwright tests\n- Art direction: engine pixel-art style, procedural shapes; no image files\n- Animation: engine Humanoid rig, E.Attack, takedown action\n- Audio: engine chip synth; layered music in code; no voices\n- Online: none\n- Testing: scripted headless Chromium checks from `file://`\n- Research: the source's public description and the engine's stealth kit\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium via Playwright\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_read_input_tokens":159849,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1730},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cdefc10-dd96-4250-9292-d55bd20762ae","uuid":"5b2966ef-6908-4f00-9a32-1e9ca622f44e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:42:40.557Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3Cf3mVVDvpuZknfe8N"}
